question(c,'A2D linear map sends(x,y) to(2x,3y). For a unit square aligned with the axes, what is the area scale factor?', [('6','The image rectangle has side lengths2 and3, so its area is6.'),('5','Adding coordinate scale factors does not give area scaling.'),('3','This accounts only for the vertical scaling.'),('2','This accounts only for the horizontal scaling.')],'Area depends multiplicatively on the two perpendicular side lengths, illustrating the determinant’s scaling role.',kind='numerical',steps=['The unit square maps to an axis-aligned2-by-3 rectangle.','Its area is2×3=6times the original unit area.'],formulas=[form('det(diag(a,b))=ab',{'a,b':'axis scale factors'})],assumptions=['Positive axis-aligned scaling in two dimensions; area, not vector length, is being compared.'])
