question(c,'Does having a zero diagonal alone prove that a real square matrix is skew-symmetric?', [('No; opposite off-diagonal entries are also required','For example[[0,1],[1,0]] has zero diagonal but does not equal its negative transpose.'),('Yes; off-diagonal entries are unrestricted','Skew-symmetry also requiresS_ij=−S_ji.'),('No; a skew-symmetric matrix must instead have diagonal1','Its real diagonal must be0, not1.'),('Yes; every zero-diagonal matrix is also the zero matrix','Off-diagonal entries can be nonzero.')],'A necessary condition is not automatically sufficient.',difficulty='hard',trap='Checking only the diagonal and ignoring opposite-pair signs.')
